6:Ta4e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the backlink monitor really free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. There is no signup and no card. You can check up to 20 pages at a time, and there is a fair hourly limit per visitor so the tool stays fast for everyone."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does it check a backlink?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We load each page the way a search engine first sees it, without running JavaScript. Then we look for every link to your domain, read its rel attribute, and check the page for a noindex tag, an X-Robots-Tag header and a canonical pointing elsewhere."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can it find every backlink to my site?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It checks the pages you give it. To find the pages that link to you, use the Links report in Google Search Console, which is free, or your own link-building records. Then paste that list here."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does a page say \"Couldn't check\"?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some sites block automated visits, some only build their content with JavaScript, and some are slow or down. In those cases we would rather say so than guess. Open the page and look for your link yourself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between dofollow, nofollow, sponsored and ugc?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A dofollow link is a normal link and can pass ranking value. Nofollow, sponsored and ugc are hints that ask Google not to pass value through the link. Those links can still bring visitors, but they help rankings far less."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I monitor my backlinks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Once a month is enough for most sites. Check new and paid links more often in their first months. Your last check is saved in this browser, so you can come back and re-check with one click."